# ── Credentials — NEVER commit ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kept in the working folder by choice; these patterns plus the pre-commit
# hook in .git/hooks/pre-commit are what keep them out of the repo (and
# therefore off the public Render site).
scripts/secrets.local.json
Social Media Account PW.md
access-and-credentials.txt

# Belt-and-braces: anything that looks like a credential file
*[Pp]assword*
*[Pp]asswords*
* PW.md
*credential*
*credentials*
*secret*
*secrets*
!scripts/secrets.local.json.example
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*

# ── Internal documents — kept LOCAL, never pushed ─────────────────────────
# The GitHub repo is PUBLIC. These hold internal strategy, personal KPI
# splits, colleagues' names and tooling plans. They stay on your machine.
social-listening-dashboard-brief.md
dashboard-explained.txt
social-api-setup.txt
social-phase2-howto.txt

# ── Build output (generated by Render, not committed) ─────────────────────
public/

